// CROWN: a function that may never return, handed to one that calls it,
// makes the caller's call one that may never return. spin counts up with
// nothing to stop it; settle says it always finishes and calls apply with
// spin. Expect E_EffectMismatch at settle, naming the recursion.
fn spin(n) = spin(n + 1)

fn apply(f, x) = f(x)

fn settle(x) with !Diverge = apply(spin, x)

fn main() = 0
